before running you will need to create a file called ".env" in the ./backend/ and another ".env" in the ./Frontend/
in the backend .env you will need the following:
    MONGO_PASS = mongo password to a DB called LLU with a users collection
    OPEN_ROUTER = you will also need an open router api key

in the Frontend .env you will need the following:
    EMAIL_USER = username of an email account that can send emails through nodemailer
    EMAIL_PASS = mail password that will let you send emails through nodemailer, THIS IS NOT THE SAME AS YOUR EMAIL ACCOUNT PASSWORD AND YOU MAY NEED TO CREATE ONE


after you have the .env files setup run the following commands:
    node setup.js
    node index.js (node) or node develop.js (nodemon)